                            <comment id="16581035" author="zjffdu" created="Wed, 15 Aug 2018 12:54:39 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;For rest api, we could provide another api which only accept paragraphId. But for websocket api (which is used by zeppelin frontend), we have to keep text, because paragraph text is not sync with backend in realtime. (Frontend will save paragraph periodically. ) That means if frontend send runParagraph websocket message to backend, backend may not have the latest paragraph text, that&apos;s why we need to send text as well. &lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16582571" author="egorklimov" created="Thu, 16 Aug 2018 14:02:30 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=zjffdu&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;zjffdu&quot;&gt;zjffdu&lt;/a&gt;, I made a simple bug fix, I think it will be better if you would provide new api as a part of your future refactoring changes.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
